<title>GERMANY: German inland gas oil eases, buyers hold off.</title>
<headline>German inland gas oil eases, buyers hold off.</headline>
<text>
<p>(DLR/DM=1.5432) DM/100 LTRS     DLRS/100 LTRS     LAST DM</p>
<p> HAMBURG	     39.10/39.50     25.33/25.59     40.90/41.30</p>
<p> BREMEN		39.10/39.50     25.33/25.59     40.90/41.30</p>
<p> DUISBURG	    39.40/39.80     25.53/25.79     41.20/41.60</p>
<p> FRANKFURT	   40.70/41.10     26.37/26.63     42.65/43.15</p>
<p> KARLSRUHE	   40.80/41.20     26.43/26.69     42.65/43.15</p>
<p> INGOLSTADT	  41.90/42.30     27.15/27.41     43.85/44.25</p>
<p>German inland gas oil eased in meagre volume on Wednesday in line with weaker IPE futures late on Wednesday and early on Thursday. Consumers were reluctant to buy, in the expectation of an imminent fall in prices. -- London newsroom +44 171 542 7646</p>
</text>
